  'consequently': <OpenCetRichExampleRow>[
    OpenCetRichExampleRow(
      exampleId: 'tatoeba:1729105:13556572',
      sourceId: 'tatoeba-cc-by-2.0-fr',
      englishText: 'Monsieur D\'Espilly, in the year 1772, calculated the population of France at upwards of 22 millions; namely, 10,562,631 males, and 11,451,726 females; consequently the proportion of females to males was about 14 to 13.',
      chineseText: '1772 年，埃斯皮利先生計算出法國人口超過 2,200 萬人；其中男性 10,562,631 人，女性 11,451,726 人；因此，女性與男性的比例約為 14 比 13。',
      englishUsername: 'shekitten',
      chineseUsername: 'LeviHighway',
    ),
    OpenCetRichExampleRow(
      exampleId: 'tatoeba:6211153:13890621',
      sourceId: 'tatoeba-cc-by-2.0-fr',
      englishText: 'We use the word "ĝi" when we are not talking about a man or a woman, but about something that has no sex or whose sex is unknown or indifferent to us. Consequently, we can almost always use this word very well in place of "tio", whose meaning is almost the same.',
      chineseText: '我们使用“ĝi”这个词，既不指男性，也不指女性，而是无性别、性别未知、或者性别无关紧要的事物。因此，我们几乎在所有情况下都可以用这个词平替“tio”，二者含义几乎一模一样。',
      englishUsername: 'carlosalberto',
      chineseUsername: 'jan_OkulaJu',
    ),
  ],
